<%- include('../partials/header', { title: 'Get the app' }) %>
<section class="install-page">
  <img class="install-crest" src="/img/logo.svg" alt="Bream Bay United AFC" width="86" height="100">
  <h1>Get the app</h1>
  <p class="install-lead">Fixtures, scores and the Cup/Plate bracket, one tap from your home screen. It's free, there's nothing to download from an app store, and it takes about 10 seconds.</p>

  <p class="install-already" data-show-for="standalone" hidden>You're already using the app - nothing more to do.</p>

  <div class="install-card" data-show-for="inapp">
    <h2>First, open this page in your browser</h2>
    <p>You're looking at this inside another app (Messenger, Facebook, Instagram or similar), and phones don't allow installing from there.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Tap the <strong>&hellip;</strong> or <strong>Share</strong> button in the corner.</li>
      <li>Choose <strong>Open in Safari</strong> or <strong>Open in Chrome</strong>.</li>
      <li>Then follow the steps for your phone below.</li>
    </ol>
    <button type="button" id="copy-install-link" class="install-btn">Copy link instead</button>
  </div>

  <div class="install-card" data-show-for="ios">
    <h2>iPhone &amp; iPad</h2>
    <p class="install-note install-note-first" data-not-browser="safari">Installing works best from <strong>Safari</strong>. If you can't see the steps below in this browser, copy the link, open Safari and paste it in.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Tap the <strong>Share</strong> button <span class="install-glyph" aria-hidden="true">&#x2B06;&#xFE0E;</span> (the square with an arrow, at the bottom or top of the screen).</li>
      <li>Scroll down and tap <strong>Add to Home Screen</strong>.</li>
      <li>Tap <strong>Add</strong>. The Twilight icon appears on your home screen.</li>
    </ol>
    <button type="button" class="install-btn install-copy" data-not-browser="safari" hidden>Copy link to open in Safari</button>
  </div>

  <div class="install-card" data-show-for="android" data-browser-group>
    <h2>Android</h2>
    <button type="button" id="install-now" class="install-btn" hidden>Install the app</button>

    <div data-browser="default chrome edge opera">
      <ol>
        <li>Tap the <strong>&#8942;</strong> menu (top right, or bottom right).</li>
        <li>Tap <strong>Install app</strong> (or <strong>Add to Home screen</strong>).</li>
        <li>Tap <strong>Install</strong>. The Twilight icon appears on your home screen.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div data-browser="firefox">
      <ol>
        <li>Tap the <strong>&#8942;</strong> menu (top right, or bottom right).</li>
        <li>Tap <strong>Install</strong>. If you don't see it, tap <strong>Add to Home screen</strong> instead.</li>
        <li>Tap <strong>Add</strong>. The Twilight icon appears on your home screen.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div data-browser="duckduckgo">
      <ol>
        <li>Tap the <strong>&#8942;</strong> menu (top right, or bottom right).</li>
        <li>Tap <strong>Add to Home Screen</strong> (it may say <strong>Add Shortcut to Home Screen</strong>).</li>
        <li>Tap <strong>Add</strong>. The Twilight icon appears on your home screen.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="install-note">If your DuckDuckGo menu has no such option, copy the link below and open it in Chrome.</p>
    </div>

    <div data-browser="samsung">
      <ol>
        <li>Tap the <strong>&#9776;</strong> menu (bottom right).</li>
        <li>Tap <strong>Add page to</strong>, then <strong>Home screen</strong>.</li>
        <li>Tap <strong>Add</strong>. The Twilight icon appears on your home screen.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <p class="install-note" data-not-browser="chrome">The icon on your home screen opens the same Twilight Football pages either way. Can't find the option? Open this page in <strong>Chrome</strong> instead and use <strong>&#8942; &rarr; Install app</strong>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="install-card" data-show-for="other">
    <h2>On your phone</h2>
    <p>This works on a phone. Open <strong><%= typeof baseUrl !== 'undefined' ? baseUrl : '' %>/install</strong> on it (or share the link below to your phone) and you'll get the right steps.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>iPhone:</strong> use <strong>Safari</strong> &rarr; Share &rarr; Add to Home Screen.</li>
      <li><strong>Android:</strong> use <strong>Chrome</strong>, <strong>Firefox</strong> or <strong>Samsung Internet</strong> &rarr; menu &rarr; Install app / Add to Home screen.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="install-card install-card-quiet" data-show-for="inapp ios android other">
    <h2>Don't want to install it?</h2>
    <p>That's fine. It's just a website: open it any time, or bookmark it.</p>
    <button type="button" class="install-btn install-copy">Copy link</button>
    <button type="button" id="share-install-link" class="install-btn" hidden>Share link</button>
  </div>

  <p class="install-back"><a class="btn btn-light btn-sm" href="/leagues">&larr; Back to the leagues</a></p>
</section>


<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
